sg-session (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Elevation consent on the secure surface (ADR 0012): sg-brokerd engages
    sg-compositor SECURE mode and runs sg-consent.exe (Yes/No for an
    administrator, an administrator's credentials otherwise); fail closed.
  * sg-vkbd test fixture (stable keymap); lock and consent gates use it.

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:47:29 -0700

sg-session (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Multi-user: supervised shell (AutoRestartShell), per-user session.env and
    logs, session checks scoped per user, machine graphics driver in HKLM.
  * Login-time Windows profile service (sg-profile-create); Default User
    template names the profile relative to %USERPROFILE%.
  * Per-user process agent (sg-procagent) for cross-process operations.
  * Elevation broker (sg-brokerd/sg-elevate), sg-admins group and sudoers.
  * Machine Group Policy: apply /etc/stained-glass/policy.d (.reg and
    registry.pol via sg-polimport) at boot; protect the policy branches.
  * Gates: token, procagent, elevate, policy.

 -- Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:00:10 -0700

sg-session (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Phase 0 session glue.
  * Bring up cage + XWayland + Wine explorer /desktop as the shell.
  * Initialize a system-wide Wine prefix at /var/lib/stained-glass/prefix.
  * Ship sg-session-check, the guest side of the image boot gate.

